    "title": "Wythe County urges residents to lock doors amid active manhunt - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Riley Johnson No media credit provided. ,\n8 hours ago\nWYTHE COUNTY, Va. ( WFXR ) –\nUPDATE: The Wythe County Sheriff’s Office has provided an updated description of the suspect on a Facebook post.\nAccording to officials, the vehicle pursuit that ended on Gardner Road involved two males in a stolen vehicle.\nThe office says that one occupant was arrested while the other ran on foot.\nThe Sheriff’s Office described the male who ran on foot as a black male wearing a white shirt and blue jeans. The last sighting of the male was on Boone Furnace Road in Pulaski County.\nThe Wythe County Sheriff’s Office is asking if you see anyone matching this description in the area, please do not approach and dial 911.\nWFXR News will update this page as more information becomes available.",
